Analyze this {language} code for concurrency and thread-safety issues.

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Race conditions (shared mutable state accessed from multiple threads without synchronization)
- Deadlocks (circular lock acquisition, lock held across blocking operations)
- Missing mutex/lock protection on shared data structures
- Channel misuse (unbuffered channels causing goroutine leaks, send on closed channel)
- Non-atomic read-modify-write on shared counters/flags
- Global mutable state modified from concurrent paths
- Context not propagated to spawned tasks (task outlives its caller)

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "issue_type": "RACE_CONDITION|DEADLOCK|MISSING_LOCK|CHANNEL_MISUSE|NON_ATOMIC|GLOBAL_STATE|CONTEXT_LEAK|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence describing the specific concurrency issue",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
